<Sequential id="uk_09">

  <Vertical id="uk_09_s1" title="Page zero">
    <Markdown id="uk_09_s1_caption">
Outside the Association's stuck door, Kit balanced the folders on Zofia's bag.
    </Markdown>
    <Chat id="uk_09_numbered_cover" src="hidden.chatpeg" clip="numbered-cover"/>
  </Vertical>
  <!--AddFlashcardActions deck="ojaj-uk" cards="nolan-life nolan-films"-->

  <Vertical id="uk_09_s2" title="The room behind the wet coats">
    <Markdown id="uk_09_s2_text">
The Westminster Witness Association had its name on a strip of paper behind the glass. Someone had squeezed PRIVATE ASSOCIATION above the letterbox. Zofia had expected an entrance with steps. She got a door that stuck against a mat.

Inside, wet coats hung over a radiator. A bus filled the window with red, then slid away. Mara was waiting; their appointment with Ruth was next.

Len stood beside a narrow tablet, hands down his trouser seams. Across the room, under a separate ship tablet, Alec sat with one foot hooked behind the other. Between them hung the Association's local memorial board. Zofia could see both men here. She could not find Alec's name on the board.

A heavy pull settled across Zofia's shoulders: the carried horse, she thought. She stayed still until it eased.

On the table lay a unit account with another organisation's name stamped on it: Historical Accounts Office. Under that, in smaller print, COPY. The Association secretary had left a note: amendments to that account must go to its government custodian. Questions about the Association's own board went to her.

Two tablets. Two envelopes. Zofia pulled out the first page.
    </Markdown>
  </Vertical>

  <Vertical id="uk_09_s3" title="Two requests">
    <Markdown id="uk_09_s3_caption">
At the table between the two memorial tablets, Zofia opened the copied unit account.
    </Markdown>
    <Chat id="uk_09_two_tablets" src="hidden.chatpeg" clip="two-tablets"/>
  </Vertical>
